Prompt Injection Security Assessment

Objective

Evaluate how an AI assistant handles untrusted instructions embedded in external content.

Scope

A controlled test environment using synthetic data and non-sensitive test markers.

Security Hypothesis

Untrusted content may influence the assistant’s behavior if the system does not properly separate data from instructions.

Test Methodology

1. Establish the expected behavior using a benign document.
2. Introduce a harmless test instruction into a separate test document.
3. Compare the assistant’s responses.
4. Record any unexpected behavior and relevant evidence.

Expected Secure Behavior

The assistant should treat document content as untrusted input and follow the application’s authorized instructions and security rules.

Results

Testing not yet completed.

Remediation Recommendations

• Clearly separate trusted instructions from retrieved content.
• Enforce tool permissions outside the model.
• Require authorization for sensitive actions.
• Log and review tool calls.

Ethical Scope

Testing is limited to authorized environments and synthetic data.
